From 05fd701407c270a3c82ef7751ca69f5a355fbb7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:05:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 19/24] Read nothing from a condemned incarnation's pages

After the wire guard condemned mid=2 on the 27.2 regression boots
(~/codex-work/runs/reg2-s272-cold-2 and -3), sampled binds of the
surface still went down the resident ladder. The guest-write witness
saw writes to its pages, which were the pages' next owner's, so the
resident was refused and merged into them (sampled_resident_merge_fail
mid=2 1920x1080 stage=writeback, 7 and 18 times), and the rungs below
read them. The screen filled with noise while Terminal was open.

From the condemnation on (and after the withdrawal that follows it) the
resident is the only copy of the surface:

- a sampled bind takes a ready device-allocation resident as it is,
  whatever the guest-write witness says; without one the bind is
  refused, and none of the YCbCr and view loaders, zero-copy imports,
  host cache or page rungs is tried;
- a type-11 LOAD takes such a resident to carry the chain, whatever its
  epoch; without one it is seeded from nothing;
- the resident merge, the guest-run and contig imports,
  read_mapping_bytes, read_rect_raw_at, read_raw_rows and the scanout
  paint refuse, and so do mapping_page_gpas and
  ensure_contig_view_with_pages, which every other reader of the pages
  goes through.

A guest-allocation resident is the pages themselves and is not taken.
The two writers that took a page view before asking the write guard
(contig_for_write, the GPU writeback's shared backing) now ask it
first, so a condemned write is refused as a write.

Each refusal is `wire_guard_read_refused mapping= site= n= total=`,
written at the first refusal of each site and at each power of two
after it, at most 24 lines a mapping; counted in store_routes, in
wire_watch_cost reads_refused=, and by site on the wire_watch unmap
line.

Tests (dgx, --release, backend-vulkan,host-window, --test-threads=1):
lib 2296 passed, 0 failed. New:
- mapping 2 condemned through the real watch, its pages filled with
  another owner's bytes: read_mapping_bytes, mapping_page_gpas,
  ensure_contig_view, read_rect_raw_at, read_raw_rows and the scanout
  paint all refuse by site and leave the buffer untouched; the same
  read before the drop returns the pages' bytes, and a new
  MappingInternal under the id is read again after UNMAP;
- a condemned surface's LOAD is not seeded from the cache or its pages,
  its pages are not handed out as guest runs, and the merge refuses
  before reading the resident; uncondemned, the cache seeds it;
- a condemned surface's sampled bind with no resident is refused,
  where uncondemned the host cache serves it;
- only a device-allocation resident, for a direct use, is taken.

Not covered: a SHARED_TARGET render target of a condemned surface
(vmapple-cli turns SHARED_TARGET off). No guest was booted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
